## 1. Biggest issue: recording matching

This is the most important problem I see.

Your current code does:

```python
f"and name contains '{meeting.meeting_title}'"
```

Then:

```python
recording = files[0]
```

So if your meeting is called:

> `recording test`

and Drive contains:

> `recording test - 2026/08/19 11:36 IST – Recording`

it works perfectly.

But imagine you have **two meetings with the same title**:

```text
English Class
English Class
```

Drive might contain:

```text
English Class - 10:00 IST – Recording
English Class - 14:00 IST – Recording
```

Your code simply takes the newest file.

That means **Meeting A could accidentally get Meeting B's recording.**

This is especially important for Appolos because repeated class titles are completely realistic.

### So:

**Recording search works technically ✅**

but

**Recording identification is not yet reliable enough ❌**

We should eventually match using something stronger than just the meeting title — ideally the actual Google Meet/Calendar relationship or recording metadata/timing.

