# 5. Your OAuth flow itself looks good

This part is actually one of the stronger areas.

You have:

```python
code_verifier = secrets.token_urlsafe(64)
```

then:

```python
authorization_url, state = flow.authorization_url(...)
```

and store:

```python
request.session["oauth_state"] = state
request.session["code_verifier"] = code_verifier
```

Then callback validates:

```python
if state != saved_state:
```

and:

```python
flow.fetch_token(
    code=code,
    code_verifier=code_verifier,
)
```

So you've got:

```text
User
 ↓
Google authorization
 ↓
OAuth state
 ↓
PKCE code verifier
 ↓
Authorization code
 ↓
Access token + refresh token
 ↓
Save credentials for user
 ↓
Django login
```

That's a sensible OAuth implementation.

