# 7. Attendance logic is actually pretty good

This section is more solid than you might think.

You are storing:

```text
Meeting
   │
   └── ParticipantAttendance
          │
          ├── ParticipantSession
          ├── ParticipantSession
          └── ParticipantSession
```

That is a good structure.

For example, if:

```text
A joins 10:00
A leaves 10:30

A joins 10:40
A leaves 11:00
```

you don't simply calculate:

```text
11:00 - 10:00 = 1 hour
```

Instead, you calculate the actual session durations.

And your:

```python
calculate_merged_duration()
```

also prevents overlapping sessions from being double-counted.

That's good thinking.

